__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Scratch, not part of the site.
#   _preview.html  the hero background picker
#   _mobile.html   horizontal-overflow audit
#   _resize.html
_hit.html

# Raw capture GIFs. gen/walkthroughs.py turns them into the mp4s that ship;
# committing both pays twice for the same frames.
assets/video/_gif/   live-resize audit
_preview.html
_mobile.html
_resize.html
_hit.html

# Raw capture GIFs. gen/walkthroughs.py turns them into the mp4s that ship;
# committing both pays twice for the same frames.
assets/video/_gif/

# The raw screen recording gen/screencaps.py cuts the walkthrough clips out
# of. Same reason as the GIFs above: every frame of it survives into the mp4s
# beside it, and committing both pays twice for one thing.
assets/video/_rec/

# One-shot scripts at the ROOT only. Anchored, because an unanchored _*.py also
# swallowed gen/__init__.py and content/__init__.py, without which `python -m gen.x`
# does not work at all on a fresh clone.
/_*.py

# NOT in the repo, deliberately. assets/fonts holds 11 commercial faces (PP Kyoto,
# ABC Diatype, Apercu Mono, P22 Mackinac, Monument Grotesk). Serving them unlicensed
# is one problem; committing them to a PUBLIC repository is redistribution, which is
# a bigger one, and git history makes it permanent.
#
# site.css @imports Newsreader, Inter, JetBrains Mono and Fraunces, and every rule
# names one of them as its fallback, so the site renders properly without these.
#
# If you buy webfont licences, or make the repo private, delete these two lines and
# run:  git add -f assets/fonts
assets/fonts/

# The persona captures BEFORE gen/persona_scrub.py repaints them. These are the
# demo seeded with real values -- a division name, an application identifier,
# a first name in the greeting -- and this is a public repository. The scrubbed
# copies in assets/tile/_src ARE tracked, so a fresh clone still builds; the
# scrub step is a no-op when this folder is absent.
assets/tile/_src/_persona/
